    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigranes-the-great">Tigranes the Great</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 83 BCE at the invitation of a faction in its civil wars and ruled it for 17 years, putting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> virtually at an end.</li><li>At its peak <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, Albania, Cappadocia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, Osroene, Adiabene, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, Judea and Atropatene, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> and some Arab tribes as Tigranes' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> became a Roman client kingdom in 66 BCE after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> defeated its ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> at the Battle of the Lycus; the last Artaxiad kings were overthrown in 12 CE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarch">Plutarch</a> say <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> was received at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxias-i">Artaxias I</a> and, in a story they also tell, planned and supervised the building of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxata">Artaxata</a>, though the tale is reckoned apocryphal.</p></aside>
    </section>

